B. Deep Learning-Aided Kalman Filters
In KN, the Kalman gain Kt(Θ), where Θ represents the set of trainable parameters, is estimated using Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs), particularly the Gated Recurrent Unit (GRU). The update equation for the KN is defined as xˆt|t = xˆt|t−1 + Kt(Θ)(yt − yˆt|t−1), where Kt(Θ) is adjusted continuously through training. For a comprehensive overview of KN, we refer to [13]. Unlike the conventional KN where a single network estimates the Kalman gain, SKN employs two separate networks. The first
